== Nerd zone ==

=== Singularity Mult Gain formula (unconfirmed) ===
<math>\frac{T}{Mult^{\frac{0.5}{STN6.1}}}</math>

where T = Total multiplier from all factors

STN6.1 = Singularity Tree Node 6.1's effect

Mult = Singularity Mult

=== Singularity Atom Requirement ===
1.79e308

if S > 10:

<math>1e320*1e20^{S-11}</math>

if S > 21:

<math>1e520*1e16^{S-21}</math>

if S > 51:

<math>1e1000*1e10^{S-51}</math>

if S > 71:

<math>10^{(S-36)^2-25}</math>

If S > 103:

<math>10^{(5082\cdot1.1^{(S-102)})}</math>

=== Singularity Effect formulas (data needed!!!1!1!1111!) ===

==== Singularity Count Effects ====
''S cooresponds to Singularity Count''

===== Gold Gain ^ =====
<math>1+0.02*S</math>

===== Atom Gain ^ =====
<math>1 + 0.005*S</math>

===== Base Spread Speed =====
<math>1 + \frac{(S+1)^2}{5}</math>

if >1000: also apply:

<math>1000 * (\frac{x}{1000})^{0.1}</math>

===== RfP Base Gain: =====
<math>10^S</math>

if >1e100, apply:

<math>10^{(100\cdot(\frac{log(x)}{100})^{0.5})}</math>

if previous result >1e250, also apply:

<math>10^{(250\cdot(\frac{log(x)}{250})^{0.25})}</math>

===== Golden Resource Gain =====
<math>(1+S\cdot 0.2)^{1.6}</math>

===== 2nd Singular Zodiac Level Multiplier =====
<math>\sqrt{1+0.1\cdot max(1,S-30)}</math>

==== Atom Count Effects ====

===== Golden Resource Gain =====
<math>1+\frac{log(A+1)^2}{10000}</math>

===== Black Gem Effect Mult =====
''A is Atom Count''

<math>A^{0.025}</math>

if >1e50, apply

<math>10^{(50\cdot\frac{log(x)}{50})^{0.4}}</math>

===== Luck ^ =====
<math>1+(\frac{log(A)-1000}{10000})</math>

==== Singularity Multiplier Effects ====

===== Base Spread Speed mult =====
''M is Singularity Mult''

<math>M^2</math>

if >1000:

<math>1000\cdot(\frac{x}{1000})^{0.1}</math>

===== RfP Base Gain =====
<math>10^{(2*log(M+1))^3}</math>

if > 1e100:

<math>10^{\sqrt{100\cdot\frac{log(x)}{100}}}</math>

if >1e250:

<math>10^{(250\cdot(\frac{log(x)}{250})^{0.25})}</math>

===== Luck ^ =====
<math>1+(\frac{log(M+1)}{25})</math>

===== First Singular Zodiac Level Multiplier =====
<math>max(1,(\frac{M+1}{25})^{0.4})</math>

=== Singularity Tree effect formulas ===
where<math>A_{x}</math>= Ascension level for STNx (internally, i.e. node 3.2 is considered node 4)

and <math>L_{x}</math> = level of STNx

and <math>n_{8}</math>= the effect of STN8

==== STN1 ====
<math>\left(1+\left(0.1\cdot A_{1}^{0.6}\right)+\frac{\left(0.01\cdot L_{1}\right)}{A_{1}+1}\right)\cdot n_{8}</math>

